      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. You mentioned extreme pH levels can have negative effects—could you elaborate on what happens when the pH goes too far in either direction? Like, does it actually stop the browning entirely, or does it just cause undesirable side reactions or even just ruin the protein structure?",
      "source": "evaluator"
